# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/events/bonds/rivals.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event lyra_rankings_war
# en: The Rankings War
title [0d42bd] = 排名之战
# en: The rankings are up outside the Great Hall. {~You're one place above Lyra.|Lyra is one place above you.} She's standing in front of the list when you get there, and she doesn't move aside. "Enjoy it," she says. "It's the last time."
text [fd298e] = 大礼堂外贴出了排名。{~你比莱拉高一名。|莱拉比你高一名。}你到的时候她正站在榜前，没有让开。“好好享受吧，”她说，“这是最后一次了。”
# en: A noticeboard outside the Great Hall with the term's rankings pinned up, two names side by side at the top, a red-haired student tapping one with her wand.
scene [641a6e] = 大礼堂外的告示板上贴着本学期排名，榜首两个名字并排，一个红发学生用魔杖点着其中一个。
# en: Out-study her this term
opt.left.label [0141b6] = 这学期在功课上压过她
# en: {~You take the library table opposite hers and don't leave it for a month. She doesn't either. Thorne remarks that he's never seen the library so tense. The next list has you in the same order. Neither of you is satisfied.|You study every night. So does she; you can see her lamp from your window. It's the best work either of you has done, and you'd both rather die than say so.}
opt.left.say.1 [d543d2] = {~你在图书馆坐到她对面那张桌子，一个月没挪窝。她也没有。索恩说他从没见过图书馆这么紧张。下一张榜上你们的名次没变。谁都不满意。|你每晚都在用功。她也是，从你的窗户看得见她的灯。这是你们俩做过最好的功课，而你们宁死也不会承认。}
# en: Leave a note on her desk
opt.right.label [57d546] = 在她桌上留张字条
# en: {~"Second suits you." She finds it in front of the whole class, and goes the colour of her hair. The next morning there's a note on yours: "Says the person who'll be third."|You leave a single word: "Close." It drives her mad for a week. It was meant to.}
opt.right.say.1 [bfeed5] = {~“第二名挺适合你。”她当着全班的面发现了它，脸红得和她的头发一个颜色。第二天早上你桌上也有一张：“说这话的人会是第三。”|你只留了两个字：“很近。”它让她抓狂了一整周。本来就是这个目的。}

@event lyra_sabotage_returned
# en: Pink Bubbles, Returned
title [527a71] = 粉色泡泡的回礼
# en: In the middle of Thorne's lecture your wand produces a cloud of blue smoke shaped like a donkey. Three rows away, Lyra is taking very careful notes. It's your move. It's always your move.
text [f09ef1] = 索恩讲课讲到一半，你的魔杖喷出一团驴子形状的蓝烟。隔着三排，莱拉正非常认真地记笔记。该你出招了。永远该你出招。
# en: A student's wand producing a cloud of blue smoke shaped like a donkey in the middle of a lecture, a red-haired student three rows away not looking.
scene [e6829e] = 课堂中途，一个学生的魔杖喷出一团驴子形状的蓝烟，三排之外一个红发学生目不斜视。
# en: Call a ceasefire
opt.left.label [664f1d] = 提议停火
# en: You slip her a note: "Truce? I'm running out of eyebrows." She reads it twice, and writes underneath: "Truce. For now. The donkey was very good though." It was.
opt.left.say.1 [55e576] = 你塞给她一张纸条：“停火？我的眉毛快不够用了。”她读了两遍，在下面写：“停火。暂时。不过那头驴真的很好。”确实很好。
# en: Escalate
opt.right.label [21c8b9] = 升级
# en: Her next spell comes out as a choir of tiny frogs singing her family motto. The whole class applauds. Lyra stands there with her wand out, absolutely white, and then, unbelievably, starts to laugh.
opt.right.say.1 [27e9db] = 她的下一个咒语变成了一群小青蛙合唱她的家族格言。全班鼓掌。莱拉举着魔杖站在那里，脸色煞白，然后，难以置信地，笑了起来。
# en: She sees it coming a mile off and turns it round. You spend detention scrubbing cauldrons. She spends it in the next room, also scrubbing cauldrons, for the donkey.
opt.right.say.2 [f93474] = 她老远就看穿了，还把它原样奉还。你在禁闭里刷坩埚。她在隔壁房间，也在刷坩埚，为了那头驴。

@event lyra_glove_thrown
# en: The Glove Thrown
title [91e54d] = 掷下手套
# en: Lyra drops a glove at your feet in the courtyard, in front of everyone. "The ring. Tonight. No referee but the crowd." She's been waiting for this all term. So, if you're honest, have you.
text [10948b] = 莱拉在庭院里当着所有人的面，把一只手套丢在你脚边。“决斗场。今晚。除了观众，没有裁判。”她等这一刻等了一整个学期。说实话，你也是。
# en: A white duelling glove on the flagstones of a crowded courtyard, a red-haired student standing over it with her wand drawn, a ring of watching students.
scene [bb50e5] = 拥挤的庭院石板上躺着一只白色决斗手套，一个红发学生拔出魔杖站在它跟前，周围一圈学生在看。
# en: Leave the glove where it lies
opt.left.label [b434b9] = 由手套躺在那儿
# en: You step over it. The crowd mutters. Lyra picks it up herself, very slowly. "Next time," she says. "There's always a next time." There is.
opt.left.say.1 [6a6d8c] = 你从它上面跨了过去。人群窃窃私语。莱拉自己把它捡了起来，非常慢。“下次，”她说，“总有下次。”确实有。
# en: Pick it up
opt.right.label [b90f6a] = 捡起来
# en: You win, barely, in front of half the school. Lyra gets up off the flagstones and, after a long moment, holds out the glove. "Keep it," she says. "Until I win it back."
opt.right.say.1 [9a0717] = 你赢了，险胜，当着半个学校的面。莱拉从石板上站起来，过了好一会儿，把手套递给你。“留着，”她说，“等我把它赢回来。”
# en: She wins, and it costs her: she's limping, and she knows you made her work for every point. "Good," she says, breathing hard. "Good. Again, soon."
opt.right.say.2 [2c079c] = 她赢了，赢得很辛苦：她一瘸一拐，也知道你让她每一分都拿得不容易。“很好，”她喘着气说，“很好。再来，快点。”

@event lyra_allies_thornwick
# en: Allies, for an Afternoon
title [3df90d] = 一个下午的盟友
# en: Three Thornwick students in green are laughing at the Lumenhold crest in the entrance hall. Lyra hears it at the same moment you do. She looks at you. You look at her. For the first time all year, you're on the same side.
text [0c0842] = 三个穿绿衣的荆木学院学生在门厅里嘲笑流明堡的校徽。莱拉和你同时听见了。她看着你。你看着她。这一年里第一次，你们站在了同一边。
# en: Two rival students standing shoulder to shoulder in a corridor facing a group of visitors in green Thornwick colours, both wands half-drawn.
scene [3f27b0] = 走廊里，两个对手肩并肩面对一群穿荆木学院绿色校服的访客，魔杖都拔出了一半。
# en: Stand with her
opt.left.label [3ba99e] = 站在她身边
# en: You stand shoulder to shoulder. The Thornwick students take one look at the two of you and remember an appointment elsewhere, though the last one flicks a jinx at your ankles on the way out, and it stings for an hour. Lyra doesn't thank you. She does walk with you as far as the stairs, which is unheard of.
opt.left.say.1 [ccd253] = 你们肩并着肩。荆木学院的学生看了你们俩一眼，突然想起别处还有约，不过最后一个走的时候朝你脚踝甩了个恶咒，疼了一个钟头。莱拉没谢你。可她陪你一直走到楼梯口，这可是闻所未闻。
# en: Let her handle it
opt.right.label [d5ddde] = 交给她处理
# en: You leave her to it and get an hour's reading done in the library. She handles it alone, magnificently, and you hear about it at dinner from four different people. "You missed it," she says, passing. She sounds as if she minds.
opt.right.say.1 [37cc3f] = 你把这事留给她，自己去图书馆读了一个钟头的书。她一个人处理了，处理得漂亮极了，晚饭时你从四个人嘴里听说了这件事。“你错过了。”她经过时说。听上去她很在意。

@event lyra_mother_watches
# en: Her Mother Watches You Win
title [0c2219] = 她母亲看着你赢
# en: An exhibition bout, and you're paired with Lyra. Up in the gallery, in black, is Lady Vaneshade. Halfway through, you're winning, clearly, and Lyra knows it, and you see her glance up once at the gallery and then not again.
text [64ce6b] = 一场表演赛，你的对手是莱拉。看台上，一身黑衣的，是凡妮希德夫人。打到一半，你明显占了上风，莱拉知道，你看见她朝看台瞥了一眼，然后再也没有看。
# en: An exhibition duelling ring with a gallery above, an elegant woman in black watching a red-haired student who is losing.
scene [e20024] = 一个表演决斗场，上方是看台，一位穿黑衣的优雅女士看着一个正在落败的红发学生。
# en: Win it
opt.left.label [1d93a6] = 赢下来
# en: You win cleanly. The gallery applauds. Lady Vaneshade doesn't. She leaves before the bows. Lyra watches her go, and then turns and shakes your hand properly. "Don't you dare go easy on me," she says. "Ever." You won't.
opt.left.say.1 [b070c8] = 你干净利落地赢了。看台鼓掌。凡妮希德夫人没有。她没等行礼就走了。莱拉看着她离开，然后转过身来，郑重地和你握手。“你敢让着我试试，”她说，“永远别。”你不会。
# en: Let her come back
opt.right.label [92da46] = 让她扳回来
# en: You slow down, just enough. Lyra wins. In the gallery, her mother nods once. Afterwards Lyra corners you, furious. "You let me," she says. Then, so quietly you nearly miss it: "Thank you. Never again."
opt.right.say.1 [b9979e] = 你放慢了一点，刚好够。莱拉赢了。看台上，她母亲点了一下头。事后莱拉把你堵在角落里，气坏了。“你让我，”她说。然后，轻得你差点没听见：“谢谢。下不为例。”

@event lyra_rival_letter
# en: A Rival's Letter
title [c65d7a] = 对手的来信
# en: A letter with the Vaneshade seal. Inside: a ruled table of her term marks, beside yours, with every subject she beat you in underlined. {~At the bottom: "Enjoy your holiday. I'm not taking one."|At the bottom: "You're welcome to check my sums. They're right."}
text [d150df] = 一封盖着凡妮希德家火漆的信。里面是一张画好格子的表，列着她这学期的成绩和你的并排，凡是她胜过你的科目都画了线。{~底下写着：“祝你假期愉快。我不放假。”|底下写着：“欢迎核对我的计算。都是对的。”}
# en: A letter with a black Vaneshade seal on a windowsill, inside it a neatly ruled table of marks with one line underlined twice.
scene [a6f1ba] = 窗台上一封盖着黑色凡妮希德火漆的信，里面一张画得整整齐齐的成绩表，有一行下面画了两道线。
# en: Write back with corrections
opt.left.label [11b838] = 回信附上更正
# en: {~You find one mistake in her sums, in your favour, and write back about it at length. Her reply is two words: "Noted. Grrr."|You send back her table with your own column added: hours slept. She doesn't answer for a week. Then: "Fine. I'll sleep. Some."}
opt.left.say.1 [db1772] = {~你在她的计算里找到一处错误，对你有利，于是写了长长的回信。她的回复只有两个字：“已阅。哼。”|你把她的表寄回去，加了一栏你自己的：睡了几个钟头。她一周没回。然后：“行。我会睡。一点。”}
# en: Pin it above your desk
opt.right.label [94c02c] = 钉在书桌上方
# en: {~You pin it up where you'll see it every morning. It works better than any timetable.|Up it goes, above your desk. Every time you want to stop, there it is, underlined twice.}
opt.right.say.1 [e590d0] = {~你把它钉在每天早上都看得见的地方。比任何课表都管用。|它被钉在了你书桌上方。每当你想停下，它就在那儿，下面画着两道线。}

@event lyra_last_match
# en: The Last Rankings
title [d8ac87] = 最后的排名
# en: The last rankings you'll ever see at Lumenhold. You and Lyra are tied. Exactly. She stands in front of the list for a long time. "Four years," she says. "And it comes to that." She doesn't sound angry. She sounds almost happy.
text [a4f700] = 你在流明堡会看到的最后一张排名。你和莱拉并列第一。分毫不差。她在榜前站了很久。“四年，”她说，“到头来就是这样。”她听上去不生气。她听上去几乎是高兴的。
# en: A final rankings list on a noticeboard, two names tied at the top, two students standing in front of it in silence.
scene [4248b8] = 告示板上贴着最终排名，榜首两个名字并列，两个学生默默站在榜前。
# en: Share it
opt.left.label [cce3a5] = 一起分享
# en: "Joint," you say. She looks at you, and then holds out her hand. You shake. "It was never going to be anyone else," she says. "I'm glad it was you I didn't beat."
opt.left.say.1 [928556] = “并列。”你说。她看着你，然后伸出手。你们握了手。“从来就不会是别人，”她说，“我很高兴没打败的那个人是你。”
# en: Ask Thorne for a decider
opt.right.label [98e038] = 请索恩出一道决胜题
# en: Thorne sets you both one question, the hardest he has. You get it by a hair. Lyra reads your answer, and nods, and says, "That's right. That's annoyingly right." She's proud of you. She'll never say it.
opt.right.say.1 [253d9e] = 索恩给你们俩出了一道题，他手头最难的一道。你以毫厘之差答对了。莱拉读了你的答案，点点头说：“对的。对得让人生气。”她为你骄傲。她永远不会说出口。
# en: Thorne sets you both one question. She gets it. You don't. She doesn't gloat, which is how you know she means it when she says, "Thank you. That's the only one I wanted."
opt.right.say.2 [21e833] = 索恩给你们俩出了一道题。她答对了。你没有。她没有得意，所以你知道她是真心的，当她说：“谢谢。我想要的就只有这一个。”

@event bram_marked
# en: Top of the Ledger
title [74cfb7] = 记过簿第一页
# en: Bram opens his demerit ledger in the middle of the corridor and writes your name at the top of a fresh page, slowly, so you can watch him do it. "A page of your own," he says. "You've earned it."
text [698e35] = 布拉姆在走廊正中翻开他的记过簿，在新的一页最上方写下你的名字，写得很慢，好让你看着他写。“专属于你的一页，”他说，“你应得的。”
# en: A big student in a red prefect's sash writing a name at the top of a demerit ledger with great ceremony, another student watching from a doorway.
scene [ac25c0] = 一个佩着红色级长绶带的高大学生郑重其事地在记过簿顶端写下一个名字，另一个学生在门口看着。
# en: Keep your head down
opt.left.label [b59315] = 低头走过
# en: You walk past without a word. He looks almost disappointed. The page stays empty for a while. It doesn't stay empty for long.
opt.left.say.1 [e26ec7] = 你一言不发地走了过去。他看上去几乎有点失望。那一页空了一阵子。没空太久。
# en: Meet his eye
opt.right.label [47716f] = 迎上他的目光
# en: You stop, and look at him, and don't look away. "Good," says Bram, and snaps the ledger shut. "I was hoping you would." It's war, and you're both, somehow, pleased about it.
opt.right.say.1 [d5df67] = 你停下，看着他，不移开视线。“很好，”布拉姆说着啪地合上记过簿，“我就盼着你这样。”宣战了，而你们俩不知怎么都挺满意。

@event bram_demerit_ledger
# en: The Demerit Ledger
title [d68875] = 记过簿
# en: Bram has given you a demerit for {~"walking in a smug manner".|"breathing in a provocative direction".} It's the fourth this month. The ledger is starting to look like a novel.
text [2cb93a] = 布拉姆给你记了一过，理由是{~“走路姿态自鸣得意”。|“朝挑衅的方向呼吸”。}这已经是这个月的第四次了。记过簿开始像一本小说了。
# en: A prefect's ledger open on a windowsill, a column of demerits next to one name, each with a reason in neat block capitals.
scene [02d917] = 窗台上摊开一本级长的记过簿，一个名字旁边列着一长串记过，每条理由都用工整的大写字母写着。
# en: Accept it with dignity
opt.left.label [eca928] = 体面地接受
# en: {~You thank him for his diligence. He has no idea what to do with that. He writes "THANKED ME" in the margin, puzzled.|You nod gravely and walk on. He follows you for a corridor, waiting for you to crack. You don't.}
opt.left.say.1 [5b126b] = {~你感谢他的尽职。他完全不知道该怎么接。他在页边写下“谢了我”，一脸困惑。|你庄重地点点头，继续走。他跟了你一条走廊，等着你绷不住。你没有。}
# en: Appeal it to his face
opt.right.label [0ead85] = 当面申诉
# en: {~You point out, with diagrams, that it's impossible to walk smugly. A crowd gathers. Bram crosses it out to make you stop.|You argue it so well that two first-years applaud. Bram crosses it out, then gives you a fresh one for "public speaking".}
opt.right.say.1 [8a64a0] = {~你画着示意图论证：走路不可能自鸣得意。围了一圈人。布拉姆为了让你闭嘴把它划掉了。|你申诉得太好，两个一年级生鼓起了掌。布拉姆把它划掉，又因为“公开演讲”给你记了一过。}
# en: {~"Arguing with a prefect," Bram says happily, writing. "That's a detention." It is.|You argue, and he writes, and the demerit becomes a detention. "Thank you," he says. "That's my quota."}
opt.right.say.2 [17aa39] = {~“顶撞级长，”布拉姆一边写一边高兴地说，“关禁闭。”确实。|你争，他写，记过变成了禁闭。“谢谢，”他说，“这下我完成指标了。”}

@event bram_inspection
# en: Inspection
title [f74fb3] = 检查
# en: "Room inspection," Bram announces, at your door, with a clipboard. There is no such thing as room inspection. He's already in. He's already opening your trunk.
text [74dcba] = “查寝。”布拉姆拿着记录板站在你门口宣布。根本没有查寝这回事。他已经进来了。他已经在开你的箱子了。
# en: A big prefect going through a student's dormitory trunk with exaggerated care, holding up a sock with two fingers, the owner standing in the doorway.
scene [43343f] = 一个高大的级长夸张地翻着一个学生的宿舍箱子，用两根手指拎起一只袜子，箱子的主人站在门口。
# en: Let him search
opt.left.label [b89090] = 让他搜
# en: He finds the kitchen's missing jar of honey under your bed. You have no idea how it got there. He does, you suspect. Detention.
opt.left.say.1 [27c00c] = 他在你床底下找到了厨房丢的那罐蜂蜜。你完全不知道它怎么会在那儿。你怀疑他知道。禁闭。
# en: He finds nothing worse than socks. He's almost disappointed. On his way out he straightens your books, without thinking, and then glares at you as if you made him do it.
opt.left.say.2 [7318b7] = 他除了袜子什么也没找到。他几乎有点失望。出门时他下意识地帮你把书摆整齐，然后瞪着你，好像是你逼他这么做的。
# en: Inspect him back
opt.right.label [492398] = 反过来检查他
# en: While he's in your trunk, you inspect his clipboard. It's mostly a drawing of a horse, quite good. You hold it up for the corridor to see. He leaves. Quickly.
opt.right.say.1 [1345c9] = 他在翻你箱子的时候，你检查了他的记录板。上面主要是一匹马的素描，画得挺好。你把它举起来给走廊里的人看。他走了。很快。
# en: He catches you reading his clipboard. "Interfering with an inspection," he says. "Detention." He covers the clipboard with his hand as he goes.
opt.right.say.2 [6083e9] = 他抓到你在看他的记录板。“妨碍检查，”他说，“禁闭。”他出门时用手捂着记录板。

@event bram_rumour
# en: The Rumour He Started
title [e30018] = 他起的谣言
# en: There's a rumour going round that you cried at the Sorting Mirror. There's a rumour that you're afraid of owls. People are being very nice to you about the owls. You know exactly where it started.
text [99239f] = 有谣言说你在分院镜前哭了。有谣言说你怕猫头鹰。大家因为猫头鹰的事对你格外和气。你很清楚谣言是从哪儿起的。
# en: Students whispering behind their hands in a corridor as one student passes, a big prefect at the far end leaning on a wall, looking innocent.
scene [4e16f6] = 一个学生走过时，走廊里的学生们捂着嘴窃窃私语，一个高大的级长靠在远处的墙上，一脸无辜。
# en: Rise above it
opt.left.label [fe2376] = 不予理会
# en: You let it run. It dies in a fortnight, as rumours do. Bram looks faintly cheated. You catch him later telling a first-year that the owl one wasn't true, quite firmly.
opt.left.say.1 [2874b4] = 你由它传。两周后它自己就消了，谣言都这样。布拉姆看上去有点被骗了的样子。后来你撞见他非常坚决地告诉一个一年级生，猫头鹰那个不是真的。
# en: Start one back
opt.right.label [b11062] = 也起一个
# en: By Friday the whole school believes Bram sleeps with a night-light shaped like a duck. He doesn't deny it fast enough. It is, it turns out, true.
opt.right.say.1 [4f67c6] = 到周五，全校都相信布拉姆睡觉要点一盏鸭子形状的夜灯。他否认得不够快。后来发现，这是真的。

@event bram_hall_tax_escalated
# en: The Hall Tax, Escalated
title [d9d876] = 楼梯税升级
# en: The hall tax has spread. There's a tin at the foot of the west stairs now, too, and a hand-lettered sign, and Bram behind it looking enormously pleased with himself. A queue of first-years are emptying their pockets.
text [706168] = 楼梯税扩张了。西楼梯脚下现在也放了个罐子，立着一块手写的牌子，布拉姆站在后面，得意得不得了。一队一年级生正在掏空口袋。
# en: A big prefect standing at the foot of a second staircase with a collecting tin, a hand-lettered sign beside him reading WEST STAIRS, a queue of first-years.
scene [3d6de2] = 第二道楼梯脚下，一个高大的级长守着一个募捐罐，旁边一块手写牌子写着“西楼梯”，排着一队一年级生。
# en: Pay, and the first-years' too
opt.left.label [9e3697] = 付钱，连一年级生的也付
# en: You drop in enough for the whole queue. The first-years look at you like you've slain a dragon. Bram looks at the tin, and at you, and for some reason shuts it. The sign is gone the next day.
opt.left.say.1 [7b41c7] = 你投进去的钱够整队人用。一年级生们看着你，像你刚屠了一条龙。布拉姆看看罐子，又看看你，不知为什么把它盖上了。第二天牌子就没了。
# en: Organise a boycott
opt.right.label [6b196e] = 组织抵制
# en: By lunch, nobody in the castle is using the west stairs. They're using the windows, a laundry chute and, in one case, a broom. Bram stands by his empty tin until dinner. Then he quietly takes the sign down.
opt.right.say.1 [80db6b] = 到午饭时，城堡里没有一个人走西楼梯。大家走窗户、走洗衣滑道，还有一个人骑了扫帚。布拉姆守着他的空罐子一直站到晚饭。然后他悄悄把牌子摘了。
# en: Nobody joins your boycott. The stairs are the shortest way to lunch. Bram waves at you, cheerfully, from behind his tin.
opt.right.say.2 [4078f4] = 没人加入你的抵制。那道楼梯是去吃午饭最近的路。布拉姆在罐子后面愉快地冲你挥手。

@event bram_after_curfew
# en: Caught After Curfew
title [b4b659] = 宵禁后被抓
# en: Bram's lantern catches you halfway up the north stairs, an hour after curfew. He smiles, slowly. He's been waiting all year for this. "Well," he says. "Well, well, well."
text [3e3aef] = 宵禁后一个钟头，布拉姆的灯光照住了半截北楼梯上的你。他慢慢地笑了。这一刻他等了一整年。“哎呀，”他说，“哎呀呀呀。”
# en: A dark castle corridor at night, a lantern held high by a big prefect, a student caught halfway up a staircase.
scene [1f37bb] = 夜里漆黑的城堡走廊，一个高大的级长高举着灯，一个学生被堵在楼梯半中间。
# en: Take the detention
opt.left.label [ca5031] = 认了禁闭
# en: "Fair," you say. It throws him; he'd prepared a speech. He writes you up. Then, as you go, he says, "Use the east stairs next time. They don't creak." You decide not to wonder why he told you.
opt.left.say.1 [351188] = “公平。”你说。这让他措手不及；他准备了一篇讲话。他给你记了一笔。然后你走的时候他说：“下次走东楼梯。那儿不响。”你决定不去想他为什么告诉你。
# en: Talk your way past
opt.right.label [f5bc3b] = 糊弄过去
# en: You tell him Professor Vey sent you for a book. He doesn't believe you. But he can't prove it, and he's not brave enough to ask Vey. He lets you go, fuming.
opt.right.say.1 [0d6c63] = 你告诉他是维伊教授叫你来拿一本书。他不信。可他证明不了，又没胆子去问维伊。他放你走了，气得冒烟。
# en: You try a story about sleepwalking. He lets you finish. Then he writes you up for curfew and for "insulting my intelligence", which he underlines.
opt.right.say.2 [0c20bb] = 你编了个梦游的故事。他让你讲完。然后以违反宵禁和“侮辱我的智商”给你记了一笔，后半句还画了线。

@event bram_rematch
# en: The Rematch
title [c607c6] = 再战
# en: Bram has been practising. Everyone knows; you've heard him on the duelling green every evening for a month. Tonight he's waiting for you there. "Last time doesn't count," he says. "Again. Properly."
text [fd5be7] = 布拉姆一直在练。人人都知道；一个月来你每晚都能在决斗草坪上听见他。今晚他在那儿等你。“上次不算，”他说，“再来。认真的。”
# en: The duelling green at dusk, a big student in a prefect's sash pulling on his gloves, a crowd forming a ring around him.
scene [1f1797] = 黄昏的决斗草坪，一个佩着级长绶带的高大学生在戴手套，周围的人群围成一圈。
# en: Not tonight
opt.left.label [4bf72b] = 今晚不行
# en: "Scared," says Bram, but he doesn't sound sure. He practises alone until dark. You can hear him from your window.
opt.left.say.1 [a8e7d7] = “怕了。”布拉姆说，可他听上去并不确定。他一个人练到天黑。你在窗前都听得见。
# en: Accept
opt.right.label [b26149] = 应战
# en: He's better. Much better. You win anyway, by one exchange. He lies on the grass looking at the sky for a while. "A month," he says. "A whole month." Then he laughs, and you help him up, and he doesn't let go of your hand at once.
opt.right.say.1 [661cf2] = 他进步了。进步很大。你还是赢了，只多一个回合。他躺在草地上看了一会儿天。“一个月，”他说，“整整一个月。”然后他笑了，你把他拉起来，他没有马上松开你的手。
# en: He wins. He stands over you, breathing hard, and doesn't gloat, and holds out a hand. "Now we're even," he says. "Now it's interesting."
opt.right.say.2 [b79cdc] = 他赢了。他站在你面前喘着粗气，没有得意，伸出一只手。“现在我们扯平了，”他说，“现在才有意思。”

@event bram_steps_in
# en: He Steps In
title [9d5d38] = 他挺身而出
# en: Two fourth-years have a first-year backed against the boathouse wall. Before you can move, Bram is there, between them, sash and all. "Problem?" he says. There are two of them, and they're bigger. He doesn't step aside.
text [64e58b] = 两个四年级生把一个一年级生堵在船屋墙边。你还没来得及动，布拉姆已经到了，挡在他们中间，绶带一样不少。“有问题？”他说。他们有两个人，而且比他壮。他没让开。
# en: A big prefect standing between two older students and a frightened first-year at the boathouse, another student arriving at a run.
scene [4eae20] = 船屋旁，一个高大的级长挡在两个高年级生和一个吓坏了的一年级生之间，另一个学生正跑过来。
# en: Stand beside him
opt.left.label [7359d5] = 站到他身边
# en: You step up next to him. One of them shoves you into the wall for form's sake, and then they decide it isn't worth it. Bram watches them go. Then he looks at you as if you've done something he can't file. "Don't make it weird," he says. He walks the first-year back to the castle himself.
opt.left.say.1 [c1e5cb] = 你走上前，站到他身边。他们中有一个为了面子把你推到墙上，然后觉得不值得。布拉姆看着他们走远。然后他看着你，好像你做了件他没法归档的事。“别弄得怪怪的。”他说。他亲自把那个一年级生送回了城堡。
# en: Run for a professor
opt.right.label [0fdbff] = 跑去找教授
# en: You bring Brask at a run. By the time you get there it's over: Bram has a split lip and the first-year is fine. He doesn't say thank you. He doesn't give you a demerit that week, either.
opt.right.say.1 [9cd2de] = 你飞奔着把布拉斯克找来了。等你们赶到，事情已经结束了：布拉姆嘴唇裂了，一年级生没事。他没说谢谢。那一周他也没给你记过。

@event bram_fathers_shadow
# en: His Father's Shadow
title [3d707b] = 他父亲的影子
# en: There's a big man in the entrance hall with Bram's jaw, talking to Bram in a low steady voice. Bram is standing very straight and getting smaller. Then the man sees you on the stairs. "Is that the one?" he says. "The one beating you?"
text [de1169] = 门厅里有个高大的男人，有布拉姆的下颌，正用低沉平稳的声音跟布拉姆说话。布拉姆站得笔直，却越来越小。然后那男人看见了楼梯上的你。“就是这个？”他说，“打败你的那个？”
# en: A big man in an old-fashioned prefect's pin standing in the entrance hall with a student who looks smaller than usual, another student watching from the stairs.
scene [e2f9bd] = 门厅里，一个别着老式级长徽章的高大男人和一个看上去比平时小了一圈的学生站在一起，另一个学生在楼梯上看着。
# en: Walk on as if you didn't hear
opt.left.label [b28ef3] = 装作没听见，继续走
# en: You keep walking. Behind you, Bram says nothing at all. That evening he finds you, and stands there, and says, "You didn't hear that." "Hear what?" you say. He nods once and goes.
opt.left.say.1 [bb83fc] = 你继续往前走。你身后，布拉姆什么都没说。那天晚上他找到你，站在那儿，说：“你什么都没听见。”“听见什么？”你说。他点了一下头，走了。
# en: Tell his father he's the best prefect here
opt.right.label [604413] = 告诉他父亲他是这里最好的级长
# en: The man looks at you as if a chair had spoken. Bram looks at you as if you've hit him. Later, he finds you. "Why," he says. Not a question. You shrug. He gives you no demerits for a month, and never says why either.
opt.right.say.1 [623d58] = 那男人看着你，像看见一把椅子开口说话。布拉姆看着你，像挨了你一拳。后来他找到你。“为什么。”他说。不是在问。你耸耸肩。他一个月没给你记过，也从没说为什么。

@event corvin_locked_out
# en: Locked Out
title [ce7443] = 被锁在门外
# en: There's a new padlock on your door. Corvin is leaning beside it, spinning a key on one finger. "Funny thing," he says. "Locks. They don't care whose side you're on. Make it worth my while."
text [4507a9] = 你的门上多了一把新挂锁。科尔文靠在旁边，一根手指转着一把钥匙。“说来好笑，”他说，“锁。它们可不在乎你站哪边。让我觉得值。”
# en: A dormitory door with a new padlock on it, a lanky student leaning beside it and spinning a key on one finger.
scene [305985] = 宿舍门上挂着一把新挂锁，一个瘦高的学生靠在门边，一根手指上转着一把钥匙。
# en: Pay him off
opt.left.label [e88f0a] = 给钱打发他
# en: He takes the coins, unlocks the door and bows you in. "Pleasure doing business," he says. He sounds tired, not pleased. The padlock is gone in the morning.
opt.left.say.1 [9ca632] = 他收下钱，开了锁，躬身请你进去。“合作愉快。”他说。他听上去很累，并不高兴。第二天早上挂锁不见了。
# en: Pick it yourself
opt.right.label [13d28e] = 自己撬开
# en: You pick it in four minutes with two hairpins. Corvin watches, and stops spinning the key. "Huh," he says. "Huh." It's the first thing he's said to you in a month that isn't a joke.
opt.right.say.1 [2a5991] = 你用两根发夹四分钟就撬开了。科尔文看着，钥匙不转了。“嗯，”他说，“嗯。”这是一个月来他对你说的第一句不是玩笑的话。
# en: You can't. He lets you struggle for twenty minutes, then unlocks it without a word and walks off. It's worse than if he'd laughed.
opt.right.say.2 [43ed52] = 你撬不开。他看着你折腾了二十分钟，然后一言不发地打开锁，走了。这比他笑出来还难受。

@event corvin_bad_odds
# en: Bad Odds
title [284112] = 不看好你
# en: Corvin is running a book on you: whether you'll fail Friday's mock paper. The odds aren't flattering. Half the common room has a coin on it. He catches your eye across the room and raises the chalk, as if to say: well?
text [81882e] = 科尔文在拿你开盘：赌你周五的模拟考会不会挂。赔率可不好看。半个公共休息室的人都押了钱。他隔着屋子和你对上视线，举起粉笔，像在说：怎么样？
# en: A chalked odds board in a dim corner of the common room, a student's name on it with long odds against them, a lanky bookmaker taking coins.
scene [8a04aa] = 公共休息室昏暗的角落里有一块粉笔写的赔率板，上面一个学生的名字赔率极低，一个瘦高的庄家在收钱。
# en: Bet on yourself
opt.left.label [42fb46] = 押自己
# en: A wager on the mock: study for it.
opt.left.hint [efcb7b] = 押模拟考：为它用功。
# en: You put your coin on yourself, at his long odds. Then you study like you've never studied. You pass the mock. Corvin pays out, every coin, and says, "Fine. I'll stop." He doesn't quite, but he shortens the odds.
opt.left.say.1 [712863] = 你按他的高赔率押了自己一枚硬币。然后你拼了命地用功。你考过了模拟考。科尔文一枚不少地赔了钱，说：“行。我不开了。”他没完全停，不过把赔率调低了。
# en: You put your coin on yourself and study all week. You pass, by one mark under his line. Corvin keeps your coin and chalks the result up with a flourish. "Close," he says. "Closer than the odds."
opt.left.say.2 [037a1d] = 你押了自己一枚硬币，用功了一整周。你考过了，却比他画的线低了一分。科尔文收下你的硬币，花哨地把结果记在板上。“差一点，”他说，“比赔率近多了。”
# en: Shrug it off
opt.right.label [9485f8] = 一笑置之
# en: You let it go. The book runs for a week and closes. Corvin wipes the board clean himself and doesn't start another. He nods to you after, which is something.
opt.right.say.1 [480113] = 你没理会。那个盘开了一周就收了。科尔文亲手把赔率板擦干净，再没开新的。后来他冲你点了点头，这也算点什么。

@event ilse_frost_door
# en: Frost on the Door
title [b53dff] = 门上的霜
# en: Your door is sealed in ice, a hand thick, clear as glass. Someone has scratched a word into the frost: a Northern word you don't know. It doesn't sound kind. In the village, they say, a girl in white furs bought nothing today, and smiled.
text [6050ce] = 你的门被冰封住了，一掌厚，像玻璃一样透明。有人在霜上刻了一个词：一个你不认识的北境词。听起来不怎么友善。镇上的人说，今天有个穿白裘的女孩什么也没买，还笑了。
# en: A dormitory door completely sealed in clear ice, a student with a kettle staring at it, a single word scratched into the frost.
scene [bc78e9] = 一扇宿舍门完全封在透明的冰里，一个学生提着水壶盯着它，霜上刻着一个词。
# en: Thaw it the slow way
opt.left.label [eabfa1] = 慢慢化开它
# en: Kettle after kettle. It takes all evening. When the last of it goes, the Northern word goes with it. You never find out what it meant, which might be the point.
opt.left.say.1 [bdf414] = 一壶接一壶。花了一整晚。最后一块冰化掉时，那个北境词也跟着没了。你永远不会知道它是什么意思，也许这正是用意。
# en: Go and find her
opt.right.label [061e72] = 去找她
# en: You find her by the frozen pond. "Your door," you say. She looks at you without blinking. "Your fault," she says. Then, after a long time, "It was a stupid word. I take it back." The ice is gone when you get home.
opt.right.say.1 [8a69ff] = 你在结冰的池塘边找到她。“你干的门。”你说。她一眨不眨地看着你。“你的错。”她说。过了很久：“那个词很蠢。我收回。”你回到家时冰已经没了。

@event ilse_contempt
# en: Beneath Her
title [5bea57] = 不屑一顾
# en: Ilse walks past you in the village square as if you were weather. Her private storm, by accident or not, empties itself into your shoes. Two villagers laugh. She doesn't look back.
text [83bc0b] = 伊尔泽在镇上广场与你擦肩而过，好像你只是天气。她的私人暴风雪，不知是不是故意，全倒进了你的鞋里。两个镇民笑了。她没回头。
# en: A girl in white furs walking past another student in the village square without looking, a gust of snow following her that soaks the other student's shoes.
scene [e122d7] = 镇上广场，一个穿白裘的女孩目不斜视地走过另一个学生身边，一阵风雪跟着她，浇湿了对方的鞋。
# en: Say her name
opt.left.label [7e575e] = 叫她的名字
# en: She stops. She doesn't turn round. "What," she says. You don't have an answer. Neither does she. But the storm over her head thins, just a little, before she goes.
opt.left.say.1 [75989f] = 她停下了，没有转身。“什么事。”她说。你答不上来。她也是。可她走之前，头顶的风雪稀薄了一点点。
# en: Let it go
opt.right.label [7a5d2f] = 算了
# en: You squelch home. It's the kind of small cold that lasts all day.
opt.right.say.1 [7ac91d] = 你一路吧唧着鞋走回去。这种小小的寒意，会跟你一整天。
